-- DOWNPORT: copied from NewEra (see ReferenceAddons); namespace localized to DragonUI_NewEra,
-- art paths re-pointed at DragonUI_NewEra\Textures\EncounterJournal. Content unchanged.
local NE = DragonUI_NewEra
-- AUTO-GENERATED by tools/gen_ej.py --flavor tbc -- DO NOT HAND-EDIT.
-- The Burning Crusade Encounter Journal, HYDRATED with real bosses + loot.
--
-- The EJ DB2 tables do NOT exist on the 2.5.5.68101 TBC client (the Encounter Journal
-- shipped in Cataclysm 4.0.1, AFTER TBC), so there is no TBC-build source. Per CLAUDE.md's
-- prime directive (retail is the source of truth) the WHOLE roster is sourced from RETAIL's
-- EJ DB2 12.0.5.67451, which covers every expansion including the Burning Crusade:
--   JournalTierXInstance/JournalInstance  -> the BC instance roster (tier 70) + names/MapIDs
--   JournalEncounter (by JournalInstanceID, OrderIndex) -> the ordered boss list + UiMapID
--   JournalEncounterCreature.CreatureDisplayInfoID      -> each boss's 3D model display id
--   JournalEncounterCreature.FileDataID                 -> each boss's boss-list portrait BLP
--   AtlasLootClassic data-tbc.lua (parse_atlasloot_tbc.py) -> ALL boss loot (dungeons + raids)
--     (the DB2 loot is the MODERN re-itemization -- Legion timewalking item ids, and for
--      dungeons a single merged table with no Normal/Heroic split; standing decision 2026-05-31
--      sources classic loot from AtlasLoot. DUNGEON rows carry diff="n"/"h" (Normal-/Heroic-only)
--      or none (both), driving the EJ difficulty dropdown; RAIDS are single-difficulty, no tag.
--      JournalEncounterItem.ItemID is the DB2 fallback for any boss AtlasLoot doesn't cover.)
--   JournalInstance.Background/Button/LoreFileDataID    -> per-instance backdrop/splash art
--   TBC LFGDungeons 2.5.5.68101                         -> per-instance entry level
--   cmangos TBCDB (tools/gen_ej_droprate.py)            -> per-item drop% (loot[].pct)
-- enc.id = JournalEncounter.ID (the EJ DB2 carries the model DISPLAY id, not a spawn npcID).
-- The Cata-era art FDIDs above are absent from the TBC client CASC, so they are extracted
-- from the retail CASC by tools/gen_ej_blps.py and registered TBC-side at the tail of this file.
--   JournalEncounterSection (Normal+Heroic, diff-tagged) -> each DUNGEON boss's ability sections
-- Outland DUNGEON abilities are EXTRACTED from the retail DB2 (un-revamped content); the 8 TBC
-- RAIDS have no retail sections and are hand-seeded in EncounterJournal/AbilitiesTBC.lua.
-- TODO(hydrate): drop%% on the ~37%% of retail-EJ loot ids the cmangos 2.4.3-era TBC DB cannot
-- price (re-itemized / badge / reputation / craft gear) -> those rows keep pct=0, no %.
--
-- Loaded by NewEra_TBC.toc AFTER EncounterJournal/Data.lua (the shared vanilla seed):
-- APPENDS these instances to NE.ej.DATA.instances, each tier=2 (Burning Crusade). The
-- encounters mirror the vanilla Data.lua schema exactly, so the existing EJ renderer shows
-- real boss pages. Era never loads this file -> the vanilla DATA + Classic continent
-- grouping in EncounterJournal.lua are untouched.
NE.ej = NE.ej or {}
NE.ej.DATA = NE.ej.DATA or { instances = {} }
NE.ej.DATA.instances = NE.ej.DATA.instances or {}
local I = NE.ej.DATA.instances
local function add(t)
  t.tier = 2
  t.encounters = t.encounters or {}
  t.shell = (#t.encounters == 0)
  I[#I + 1] = t
end

